```js
const res = await db.collection('products').findOneAndUpdate(
  { _id: productId, stock: { $gte: qty } },
  { $inc: { stock: -qty } },
  { returnDocument: 'after' }
)
if (!res) throw new Error('Out of stock')
```
(With the Node driver v6+, `findOneAndUpdate` returns the document directly by default.) If decrementing stock and creating the order must succeed or fail together, wrap both in a **transaction**, or design so the order can be compensated if the second step fails.
